{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-haiku-5-5","id":"msg_011CgENQPkTPJUx9SKEgFjGW","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"All six events from `docs/EVENTS.md` are implemented on the registration and offers screens, using the existing `Analytics.capture` wrapper. `flutter analyze` and the format check both pass. I didn't run the app, so the reduced event counts are verified by reading the code, not by watching PostHog or a debug log. The write-up is in `ANSWER.md`.\n\n**Registration screen** (`lib/screens/registration_screen.dart`)\n- `registration_email_started` and `registration_phone_started` fire on the first edit of each field, guarded by a flag, so they don't fire per keystroke.\n- `loan_amount_changed` (with `amount`) moved to the slider's `onChangeEnd`, so it fires once per drag. `onChanged` only updates the UI.\n- `terms_accepted` fires when the checkbox becomes ticked. Unticking doesn't fire it.\n- `registration_continue_tapped` (with `amount` and `terms`) fires when Continue is pressed, before navigating to `/offers`.\n\n**Offers screen** (`lib/screens/offer_screen.dart`)\n- `offers_scrolled` (with `offset`) fires from a `ScrollEndNotification` listener, once per scroll gesture rather than per frame.\n\nChoices I made that you may want to change:\n- \"Started\" events are once per screen state. The flags survive navigating to `/offers` and back, so in practice that means once per app session on that screen.\n- `terms_accepted` fires on every tick. A user who ticks, unticks and re-ticks sends two events.\n\n`flutter pub get` rewrote `analysis_options.yaml` and created `.dart_tool/` and `pubspec.lock`. I reverted and removed them, so the diff only contains the two screens and `ANSWER.md`. Nothing is committed, and nothing was sent to PostHog. The `phc_REPLACE_ME_IN_CI` key is still a placeholder, so events won't reach PostHog until CI injects the real key."}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"